From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:45:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] tools: asahi: host suite for the T6001 AGX vote policy, with
 mutant controls

The vote policy is a header of static inline transition functions, so the
suite compiles pmp-agx-vote-tests.c against a copy of it and drives the same
begin, decide, next and applied calls the kernel glue makes, with a fake
clock, a fake PMP bit and a fake timer. 18 cases: the parameter off, the set
and idle drop, decode-like bursts, a drop cancelled by new work, the failed
set backoff, unbalanced ends, the parameter switched off mid-flight, the zero
idle tick, millisecond clock wraps, release and refuse, resume with and
without work in flight, sleep and resume, and the two asserts from review
(the begin inside a clear write must be re-set, and begin must refuse while
stopped).

--mutation and --mutations remove one guard each (the owed-set branch, the
!failures in it, and the stopped check in begin and decide) and require the
suite to fail. The two mutants that survived before the races fix (begin not
refusing while stopped, and the retry deadline indistinguishable from the 1 ms
owed-set kick) are the stopped-in-begin and owed-set-branch controls: at
5b54de31 (the pre-fix header) both survive because the guarded lines do not
exist; at this head each is caught at the case that pins it.

Registered in tools/aurora-ci/host-tests.json (base, --mutations, four
single-mutant entries, the .c as a helper).

Proof: plain run passes (18 cases, AGX-VOTE-SELFCHECK-OK); --mutations exits 0
with all four caught; --ref 5b54de31 --mutation stopped-in-begin and
--mutation owed-set-branch print SURVIVED there.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1142df92a11668749f5946f69f5f1b48e20153c5)
